Subject: [DRAFT, not in series] stamp every stage line with at=<sec>.<ms>

Draft only. Deliberately not in patches/*/series, not built, not flown.

Why: the zero-copy criterion cannot say "the panel was fed for three seconds".
It can only say "the frame counter advanced", because the stage line carries
spans but no absolute time, so no window can be placed on a clock (see
docs/research/gpu/GPU-27-JUDGE-DRAFT.md 8.5 and k60-gates
scripts/check-gpu27-zero-copy.py, rule 5).

Three properties this draft is built around:

  1. one clock, read once. The stamp reuses t1, the CLOCK_MONOTONIC reading the
     wait span already takes, so the loop takes no second reading for a field.
     A failed reading keeps the previous frame's stamp instead of inventing 0.
  2. appended at the end of the line, so no group in the judge's STAGE regex
     moves (P-295: an inserted optional group renumbered every capture behind
     it and the judge silently read submit as gpu).
  3. absent means "no window can be judged", never "the window held". The gate
     exits 2 when the field is missing, which is why this draft is harmless to
     carry and useless to fake.

Apply order: stacks on pong-metal-client-gap.patch - both edit the same report
block, so this diff is written against the tree that already has 0002. Apply
0002 first, then this; applied to a tree without 0002 it does not apply, and
that is the dependency talking, not a broken patch (same shape as
pong-scanout-v2-layout-asserts.patch needing the offset patch).

--- a/drivers/PongMetal/PongMetalScanout.h
+++ b/drivers/PongMetal/PongMetalScanout.h
@@ -34,6 +34,11 @@
      * two as if they were the same number. `previous` is the arrival time of the
      * frame before this one, so the first frame reports 0 and is not a sample. */
     struct timespec previous={};uint64_t lastGap=0;
+    /* When this frame arrived, on the clock the wait span already read: the
+     * window rule needs two lines that can be placed on one timeline, and the
+     * three spans on this line are durations, not instants. A failed reading
+     * keeps the previous stamp; the field is never printed as an invented 0. */
+    uint64_t lastAt=0;
     pthread_set_qos_class_self_np(QOS_CLASS_USER_INTERACTIVE,0);
     for(;;) {
         @autoreleasepool {
@@ -51,6 +56,10 @@
                 const uint64_t gap=span(previous,t1);
                 if(gap)lastGap=gap;
                 previous=t1;
+                /* t1 is this frame's arrival, already read for the span above:
+                 * one clock, one reading, so at= and client= describe the same
+                 * timeline. */
+                if(stamped(t1))lastAt=absoluteUs(t1);
             }
             auto result=context->presenter->present({reinterpret_cast<void *>(frame.address),size_t(frame.bytes),
                 size_t(frame.stride),frame.width,frame.height});
@@ -158,13 +167,14 @@
                  * divided by 1000 while still carrying the "us" label, which made a 48 ms frame
                  * read as a 48 us copy and turned P-234 into a false "the copy is free" verdict. */
                 char rate[640];snprintf(rate,sizeof(rate),
-                    "scanout frames=%u at %llu.%03llu s; last frame: wait=%llu us copy=%llu us done=%llu us client=%llu us; imports=%llu import=%llu us encode=%llu us submit=%llu us gpu=%llu us sum=%llu us",
+                    "scanout frames=%u at %llu.%03llu s; last frame: wait=%llu us copy=%llu us done=%llu us client=%llu us; imports=%llu import=%llu us encode=%llu us submit=%llu us gpu=%llu us sum=%llu us at=%llu.%03llu",
                     copies,(unsigned long long)absoluteUs(now)/1000000ull,(unsigned long long)(absoluteUs(now)%1000000ull)/1000ull,
                     (unsigned long long)lastWait,(unsigned long long)lastCopy,(unsigned long long)lastDone,
                     (unsigned long long)lastGap,
                     (unsigned long long)context->presenter->imports(),
                     (unsigned long long)imported,(unsigned long long)encoded,(unsigned long long)submitted,
-                    (unsigned long long)waited,(unsigned long long)(imported+encoded+submitted+waited));
+                    (unsigned long long)waited,(unsigned long long)(imported+encoded+submitted+waited),
+                    (unsigned long long)lastAt/1000000ull,(unsigned long long)(lastAt%1000000ull)/1000ull);
                 report(rate,0);
             }
         }
